INT. BACKSTAGE, SUBMARINE-THEMED MUSEUM GIFT SHOP - NIGHT

A cramped storeroom of plush squid, periscope keychains, and cardboard boxes marked FRAGILE. A string of party lights hangs over a folding table of wilting cupcakes.

ELOISE VANTERPOOL (30s, rolled-up sleeves, name tag reading "Ask Me About Barnacles") counts stock with a clicker. At the doorway, ROMAN ASTOR-LIN (30s, rumpled blazer, wet from the rain) lingers with a bouquet of grocery-store carnations.

ROMAN
Hi.

ELOISE
You're late.

ROMAN
I know.

ELOISE
By three years, in fact.

ROMAN
(quietly)
I know.

She keeps clicking. He sets the carnations on the table, beside a cupcake that has "CONGRATS" piped across it in blue.

ROMAN (CONT'D)
Whose party?

ELOISE
Retirement. Dr. Penhallow. Thirty-one years of squid.

ROMAN
I came to see you.

ELOISE
Ro, don't.

ROMAN
Eloise, listen. I didn't leave because I wanted to. My mother got sick, I flew to Singapore, and every time I tried to write the letter it came out like a lie. So I stopped trying. And then it was a year. And then it was too long.

ELOISE
You could have called.

ROMAN
I could have done a lot of things. I'm not asking you to forgive me. I'm only asking you to let me stand here for a minute.

She stops clicking. She sets the clicker down and finally turns.

ELOISE
Your mother?

ROMAN
She passed in March.

ELOISE
(softer)
I'm sorry.

ROMAN
Thank you.

ELOISE
Ro...

ROMAN
Yeah?

ELOISE
You still have that stupid scarf?

ROMAN
(laughing, relieved)
It's in the car.

Laughter from the corridor. A door bangs open and a crowd of coworkers fills the storeroom with noise. At the front, a new arrival: DR. HESTER PENHALLOW (60s, tweed, bow tie shaped like a seahorse), glowing with champagne.

PENHALLOW
Eloise! There you are! Is this the famous Roman?

ELOISE
(blushing)
Dr. Penhallow, he's not--

PENHALLOW
You've been talking about him for three years. Have a cupcake, dear boy.

Roman looks at Eloise. She does not meet his eyes, but she does not deny it.

ROMAN
Thank you. I will.

Behind them, a grinning intern, COLM BRADSHAW (20s, lanyard, hopeful), holds up a phone.

COLM
Group photo! Everyone squeeze in!

Eloise steps beside Roman. Their shoulders touch. Neither moves away.

ELOISE
(low)
You're buying dinner.

ROMAN
(low)
Anything.

ELOISE
(low)
Anywhere?

ROMAN
(low)
Anywhere.

Colm's flash goes off. For one frame, they are both laughing.

PENHALLOW
Lovely. Now, who wants to hear about the giant squid?

Groans from everyone. Eloise leans against Roman and whispers.

ELOISE
Run.

They slip out through the storeroom's back door. The party lights keep swaying behind them.
